  "step_1": "The decision reason evaluates lotteries based on the probability of obtaining a favorable outcome. A favorable outcome is defined as receiving a positive amount (i.e., more than 0 Euros). In Lottery A, the outcome is 2400 Euros with 100% probability, so the probability of a favorable outcome is 100%. In Lottery B, the favorable outcomes are 2500 and 2400 Euros, occurring with probabilities 33% and 66%, respectively. The 1% chance of 0 Euros is considered unfavorable. Therefore, the total probability of a favorable outcome in Lottery B is 33% + 66% = 99%. Thus, Lottery A has a 100% probability of a favorable outcome, and Lottery B has 99%. The decision reason states that differences in outcomes are negligible and that the lottery with the higher probability of a favorable outcome is preferred. Therefore, the reason applies and compares the probabilities of favorable outcomes: A (100%) vs. B (99%). The reason would prefer A over B due to the higher probability of a favorable outcome.",
